  "subject": "⚾️ Axios Finish Line: 4 winning rules",
  "date": "Mon, 02 Nov 2026 21:29:24 -0500",
  "body_text": "96 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n 🏞️ Plus: Utah's Mighty 5 | Monday, November 02, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n View in browser \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n Axios Finish Line \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n By Mike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei &middot; Nov 02, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n Welcome back! Smart Brevity™ count: 486 words … 2 mins. Edited by Natalie Daher and copy edited by Amy Stern. \n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 1 big thing: Be like Pat Murphy \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Photo: Daniel Shirey/MLB Photos via Getty Images Pat Murphy, who just led the Milwaukee Brewers to their first World Series title in franchise history, is the leader all of us should be, Axios' Jim VandeHei writes. \n\n 🏆 Why it matters: Too many loud-mouth, self-centered leaders light up our screens and the internet. Murphy shows you can be the very best at what you do on the planet — and still be a good person, with a big heart and great values . For those of us on the back nine, he shows it's never too late: He didn't get his first full-time, big-league managing job until 65.\n\n The big picture: Murphy didn't win with stars or sluggers. In fact, he broke many of the \"conventional\" rules. The Brewers won 103 games, then went 11-2 in the postseason, mostly without the long ball.\n\n He built a culture — and the culture won a championship. ⚾️ Murphy's playbook is made up of four principles any of us can steal:\n\n 💛 Love first, then discipline. \"I believe in love and discipline — in that order,\" he said the day he was introduced. He pulled star catcher William Contreras from a game for not running hard, and the next day, they laughed about it together when Contreras slid into first and smiled at the boss. Countless times he just looked a player in the eyes and said, \"I believe in you.\" Even high-achieving adults need to hear that. 🧢 Gamers beat Hall of Famers. After sweeping the Dodgers: \"They may have a bunch of Hall of Famers, but we've got a bunch of gamers.\" What he means here: Hire for talent and character. A team of grinders who trust each other beats a collection of self-obsessed stars. 🌟 Get the small things right. We tend to think and talk about nailing the big things, but it's the small things that make big things possible. Elite organizations do the unglamorous work right every day. The Brewers are obsessed with finding and grooming overlooked talent, mastering little edges like stealing bases or simply putting the ball in play over pure power. 😟 \"Worry is a waste of time.\" Murphy brings his kids to press conferences and says they pray each night they — and he — don't worry. His point is to focus on the now, the controllable. Don't get stuck in the negative headspace of what could theoretically go wrong later. 🐐 The bottom line: Go Brewers.\n\n Share this story . \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\nA MESSAGE FROM AXIOS\r\n\n \r\n See what's next for media in 2027 \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n Media Trends Executive Annual members receive the 2026 Annual Report, our special media document featuring global forecasts, sector analysis and exclusive media data insights.\r\n\n\r\n \r\n🔒 Get the report by becoming a Media Trends Executive member.\r\n\n\r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 2. 📸 America&#x27;s natural wonders \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Photo: Bruce Bosse Axios reader Bruce Bosse of Knoxville, Tenn., and his wife, Sharon, recently spent 10 days visiting Utah's \"Mighty 5\" national parks: Zion (pictured above), Bryce Canyon, Capitol Reef, Arches and Canyonlands (below).\n\n \"While we love our international travels, the national parks we have in the United States are true gems!\" Bruce writes. Photo: Bruce Bosse 🏜️ Here's Mesa Arch in Canyonlands National Park, photographed just after sunrise.\n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n 🏁 Please invite your friends to join Finish Line . \n\n \r\n 👆 Like this comms style and format? It's called Smart Brevity®. Bring it to your org — via hands-on training or internal comms software — to harness its power and impact. \r\n &nbsp; Axios thanks our partners for supporting our journalism.\n Advertise with us. \n\n Read more about Axios' mission , ethics and how we use AI in our journalism . You can reach the authors by replying to this email.\nSponsorship has no influence on editorial content.\n\n Thank you for signing up for this Axios newsletter. To stop receiving this newsletter, unsubscribe or manage your email preferences . If someone forwarded this to you, sign up now to get Axios in your inbox.\n\n Axios, PO Box 101060, Arlington VA 22201 &nbsp; Follow Axios across:\n\n &nbsp; &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;",
